::SQL Alias::
What is the output of the following SQL statement?
SELECT Emp.Emp_ID, First_name, Last_name
FROM Emp e1, Emp2  e2
WHERE e1.Emp_ID = e2.Emp_ID
{
    ~A list of all employee IDs and their First_name and Last_name
    =Error - If Aliasing is used, it must be used throughout
    ~A list of matching employee IDs and their First_name and Last_name
    ~None of the above
}

::Question::What is the purpose of the SQL AS clause?
{
   ~The AS clause defines a search condition
   ~The AS clause is used with JOIN clause only
   =The AS SQL clause is used to change the name of a column in the result set or to assign a name to a derived column
   ~All of the above
}


